 "doc": "Ch4 'The Pilgrim's Wake' (M3-C04-02; docs/kb/story/beats/act1_ch04.md C4-01 to C4-15; docs/kb/tech/chapter_flow.md 'Ch4'). Two greybox zones, played by ZoneStory. ch04/haluna_wake is a stand-in for ch02/haluna's night variant (HalunaStory is not data-driven, ADR 0035): it opens once B11 has sworn Rhen in (ch03_rhen_sworn_guardian; the slice's end card stays the M2 build's ending, and the full game's hand-off is the end card's next_location, M3-C04-04). C4-01 moves the story to chapter 4 (the chapter autosave), seats Rhen, Asha and Toma, and plays the lamps going to the wall; the windows go dark after it. C4-02 is the dark town loop and its barks; C4-03 the walkable feast (Ysolde's hold on the way in, four tables, Neme's the one the wall waits for); C4-04 and C4-05 the shell set and Rhen walking out; C4-06 the dark dock (the Kell choice); C4-07 'The Ink' at the wall, optional; Neme's door ends the night: C4-08 the dawn causeway, then ch04/brightwater_ferry at Landing. The ferry: C4-09 the gangplank (Ysolde joins, in reserve: the field party is Rhen, Asha and Toma with Ysolde in reserve), C4-10 the crossing (three overheard banters, the purser's shop, the deckhouse shrine as a rest: GreyboxZone has no SaveShrine yet), no battles on the ferry, ever (ADR 0017 (d)); C4-11 at the bow, the Seventh Terrace and the crossing to her; C4-12 the derelict (the leech ambush, the barks, the bottle-hermit lesson with Ysolde in reserve whatever the formation, random fights only aboard her); C4-13 the Spar-Wraith after a breath (a full heal, as Ch1 before Hullgnaw: its band assumes a full party); C4-14 the name-board (key item name_board_seventh_terrace) and C4-15 under way. Ch5's ch05/pemakar is not on this branch yet, so the chapter hands on to the end card as a stand-in; repoint the last step to {\"go\": {\"location\": \"ch05/pemakar\", \"spawn\": <its harbour spawn>}} when Ch5 merges (M3-C04-04).",
